hotty-blitz's new effects: a field's cut puts its text on the clipboard,
and a field's paste reads the clipboard with paste_from_clipboard, after
the key, once the renderer lock is let go. While a surface's text field
has the keyboard, completeClipboardPaste types what is pasted into it,
the terminal's own paste included (Control+Shift+v, Command+v), instead
of writing it to the pty; a paste then asks for text, not kitty's paste
event. Undo is the field's own, in hotty-blitz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
